This is the gold dropping bug. It works in all current Mac 3.0 versions
and really any version that is 3.0. It is a bit of classified info, so
if you don't feel up to it, hit n now.
























The infinite gold dropping bug.

First, you have to have gold in your inventory to make it.
Make sure you have at leats one coin.

Then hit d for drop

Hit 1 for number of things to drop

Hit Z or some other letter to represent an item NOT in your inventory

It may say more, if so hit return

Then hit $ for gold

It will say "You drop 0 gold coins"

Then pickup with ,

You'll have more than you did before. Guaranteed.

For those that like to program macros, do "d1Z$," or "d1Z [Return] $,"

THAT'S the gold dropping bug. ;) And I really didn't want to call
the /dev team a bunch of idiots. I just think they could have
waited a bit longer and made a much better version of NetHack 3.1 for
